==In the TCG==
[[File:SchoolgirlFusionStrike262.jpg|200px|thumb|Full Art print of Schoolgirl]]
{{main|Schoolgirl (Fusion Strike 239)}}
'''Schoolgirl''' was introduced as a {{TCG|Supporter card}} in the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] during the English Sword & Shield Series (the Japanese Sword & Shield Era). It was first released in the Japanese {{TCG|Skyscraping Perfection}} expansion before debuting in English in the {{TCG|Fusion Strike}} expansion, with an illustration based on the [[kirisAki]] artwork of the character. It was also released as a {{TCG|Full Art card}} and {{TCG|Secret card}} in both expansions, with an illustration by [[Hideki Ishikawa]]. Schoolgirl allows the player to draw 2 cards, and if the opponent has exactly 2, 4, or 6 Prize cards remaining, 2 more cards are drawn.
{{-}}

